The goal of this project is to move from reactive customer support to proactive, intelligent service operations using the capabilities of Salesforce.

In traditional systems, issues are only addressed after a customer reports them, leading to downtime, poor experience, and delayed resolution. This project aims to solve that problem by building a system that can detect, predict, and act on potential failures before they happen.

By simulating real-time device data and applying an AI-driven decision layer, the system continuously monitors device health, identifies risks early, and automatically initiates actions such as case creation after a time and customer notification—without waiting for manual intervention.

Additionally, the project connects service operations with business value by identifying repeated failures and generating sales opportunities, demonstrating how support systems can also contribute to revenue growth.

Overall, the objective is to showcase how modern systems can become autonomous, data-driven, and customer-centric, improving both operational efficiency and user experience.
